---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JournalEntryLayout from '../../components/JournalEntryLayout.astro';
import JournalIllustration from '../../components/JournalIllustration.astro';
import '../../styles/notes.css';
import '../../styles/note-entry.css';

const previewDate = new Date('2026-10-03T12:00:00');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Finding Brambley | Entry Template Preview"
  description="Approved Brambley journal entry template preview."
  bodyClass="notes-page-body"
>
  <JournalEntryLayout
    title="Finding Brambley"
    date={previewDate}
    subtitle="A bit of luck, a lot of looking, and a place that felt right."
    category="chronicle"
  >
    <p>
      What began with a California tax bill turned into a four-year search. I knew I wanted
      land, trees, and water, but I wasn’t sure where. I spent a lot of time looking at maps,
      reading about different areas, and driving more back roads than I can count. Most
      places were close, but not quite right.
    </p>

    <p>
      The first time I drove down the lane at Brambley, I remember thinking that it felt
      different. The meadows, the alder trees, the pond, and the way the light came through
      the trees all felt like the right mix. It needed work, but that was part of the appeal.
      There was room for gardens, an orchard, and a hundred small projects.
    </p>

    <JournalIllustration
      src="/assets/notes/entry-landscape-approved-2x.webp"
      alt="Watercolor landscape looking across meadow and water toward wooded hills"
      caption="Looking across the meadow toward the harbor."
      width="wide"
    />

    <p>
      There have been plenty of challenges since then, from blackberry canes to drifting alder
      seedlings, but the good days far outnumber the hard ones. Every season brings something
      new to notice, and there is always another project waiting.
    </p>

    <p>I wouldn’t have it any other way.</p>
  </JournalEntryLayout>
</BaseLayout>
